# scry-on-turn with nothing to look at: Bot1's library is empty on its first upkeep (its whole deck is its opening hand), so
# "scry 3" looks at no cards and asks nothing (CR 701.22a: the top cards, of which there are none); the ability resolves and
# the turn goes on. Bot1 plays first and does not draw on turn 1 (CR 103.8a), so nothing else empties into a loss.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest x7

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x40

[Variant]
Bot1: emblem Gear test: scry-on-turn, turn 1, count 3

[Actions]
[T1 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Stack = Gear test: scry-on-turn, turn 1, count 3
[T1 Bot1.Main1]
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Library.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
Bot1.Status = (absent)
